# Belt-and-braces only. The real guarantee is vercel.json's
# "outputDirectory": "public" — the publish directory holds ONLY the site
# (index.html + catalog.js + 404.html), enforced by test_publish_dir.py.
#
# History, so nobody re-widens the scope: outputDirectory used to be "." and
# Vercel published the whole repo root (648 MB / 593 files, including the
# gitignored data_cache/). .vercelignore is the ONLY list Vercel reads — it does
# NOT honour .gitignore — so .claude/settings.local.json and
# .claude/skills/**/SKILL.md served 200 in production, and CLAUDE.md and
# refresh.sh were still serving 200 after those were added here. A deny-list you
# have to remember to update is the wrong shape; the publish directory is the fix.
.claude/
.playwright-mcp/
.vercel/
__pycache__/
data_cache/
harvest/
*.pyc
*.py
*.sh
*.yaml
*.md
.DS_Store
file_profiles.json
file_profiles.prev.json
requirements.txt
